steps.instructions:
Owner direction (docs/00_brief.md п.33–35): match the reference frames docs/reference/ref1..ref5 in composition and world content, in the soft cartoon style «Raivon Soft» (docs/art_direction.md §6; §5 for world content). Read keys A1_fresh_look_fix, A1_fresh_look_review2 and Z1_art_followups_review and the backlog item «Арт-проход 6 (хвосты A1)» in docs/dev/backlog.md. Candidates, rank them by impact on the strategic view a player sees most (shoot DL1/DL3/DL5/DL7 strategic and close with tools/godot_shot.sh and put each next to the matching reference frame first):
- forests: a third spruce and denser dark conifer masses (ref1);
- mountains: a ridge or saddle between the massifs (they read as rounded standing stones, not a ridge of peaks as in ref1/ref3); foot variants per biome (taiga, barren) — today one baked surface, so only separate models can recolour the foot;
- quarry/mine: stepped tiers of straight cut blocks (ref4) instead of rounded boulders;
- the DL1 capital (a «haystack» tent; its building card renders from the same model — re-render the card with tools/blender/card_art.py only through its documented CLI if the model changes, or list it as a follow-up);
- aviation over armies (gunship angular up close, too small at strategic zoom), the destroyer (a thin strip at strategic zoom);
- oil crude colour: oil_l1..l4 use #3E3A5C, the dark lake moved to #45406A — sync it (10.8 % of the pond box under L* 15);
- the mountain in front hides most of the marauder camp in ch2:camp at zoom 0.12 (a placement change: write it as a patch).
Fix the top 4–6 in Blender (soft materials, baked AO per §6.5, correct scale and seating), re-export only the touched models, import under the lock, verify in game at the same views (before/after pairs next to the reference frames). PERFORMANCE: the strategic overview is already over budget (ch2:view 3D+shadow 407, battle DL8 394, budget ~330 — step R1 fixes it after you): your models must not add draw calls or shadow casters there — keep triangle counts within each script's notes, one material/surface where possible, and say per model how many surfaces/draws it costs before/after. Every map_view.gd change (placement, biome choice, new model names) goes into scratchpad/polish/AP6_art_pass6/followup_*.patch, exact and tested with `git apply --check` against the current tree, listed in your report — step R1 applies them. Whatever your role (implementer, reviewer, fixer), ALSO write your final structured result as JSON to scratchpad/polish/AP6_art_pass6/report_<role>.json (report_impl, report_review, report_fix, report_review2, report_fix2) before you return.
